diff --git a/source/json.html b/source/json.html
index 00700b5da67..c5a8aa9aacc 100644
--- a/source/json.html
+++ b/source/json.html
@@ -95,7 +95,11 @@ e.g.,
 <p>
 The <code>resourceDefinition</code> property is a feature of the JSON format, and is not defined anywhere 
 in the structural definitions of FHIR (in the same way that the <code>resourceType</code> property is not).
-The resourceDefinition property is not present if the resourceType is one defined in this specification.
+The resourceDefinition property is not present if the resourceType is one defined in this specification,
+except that if an additional resource has moved into this specification, existing instances are allowed
+to retain the property for backwards compatibility. It SHOULD NOT be added to new instances once the
+resource is defined in this specification. If present for such a moved resource, its version SHALL be
+correct with regards to the published core FHIR version.
 </p>
 <a name="repeat"></a>
 <h3>JSON Representation for repeating elements</h3>
diff --git a/source/resource/resource-introduction.xml b/source/resource/resource-introduction.xml
index 50e0adcf684..36d3f48f270 100644
--- a/source/resource/resource-introduction.xml
+++ b/source/resource/resource-introduction.xml
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ Generally, the process for moving an Additional Resource to core is:
  <li>The resource will be added to the next ballot of FHIR core.</li>
  <li>The resource will be officially available when the milestone release that includes it is published.</li>
  <li>Concurrently with that FHIR Core publication, the status of the 'additional' definition should be updated so that it is deprecated and then eventually removed</li>
- <li>Once the resource has been moved to core, the <code>resourceDefinition</code> element defined for XML and JSON is allowed to remain present, but SHOULD NOT be added.
+ <li>Once the resource has been moved to core, the <code>resourceDefinition</code> JSON property or XML attribute is no longer needed. It is allowed to remain present for backwards compatibility, but SHOULD NOT be added.
     If it is present, the version SHALL be correct with regards to the published core FHIR version</li>
 </ul>
 
